    {
      "abstract": "FIG. 6: \u201c(Color online)\u201da) left side: The charge dependent (CD) signal shape is a 2 dimensional (2-D) approximate gaussian which is symmetrical. The average gaussian width is 27.5$^{\\circ}$ $\\pm$ 3.2$^{\\circ}$ (0.48 $\\pm$ 0.056 rad) both in $\\Delta\\phi$ and $\\Delta\\eta$. Thus we are observing a greater probability for unlike-sign charge pairs of particles than for like-sign charge pairs emitted randomly on 2-D $\\eta\\phi$ directions. b) right side: The CD signal data corresponding to the adjacent signal fit on the left.",
